  "answer": "The KX-100 can't do this measurement, for two separate reasons. First, its frequency range is 10 MHz to 18 GHz, so it can't give a calibrated reading of a 40 GHz signal; SENS:FREQ refuses any value above 18 GHz with error -222. Second, its resolution is 0.01 dB (FETC? returns two decimals), so it can't give 0.001 dB, and no setting or averaging count changes either limit. You'll need a power meter and sensor rated for 40 GHz that reads to 0.001 dB.",
  "quote": "A reading finer than the resolution is not available from the instrument, and a signal outside the frequency range cannot be measured with a calibrated result."
}

